lf: Sulaiman (AD 851) states of the Gurjara king that \'no other Indian prince has so fine a cavalry . . \'his camels and horses are numerous.\' Ghoshal comments that the Indian authorities of both this period and the later eleventh-twelfth centuries agree in assigning \'the first rank in their classified list of horses to the foreign breeds, and the lowest to the indigenous breeds.\' The former indicates well-established trade links."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2068, 'temperature': 0.2})
